<div class="abe-section-block" data-block-type="FancyBlockSection" data-block-id="">
<table class="abe-section-table" style="max-width: 600px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;" role="presentation" border="0" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" align="center">
<tbody>
<tr id="abe-section-row-a1ded004-e27a-4407-a278-7aacf8bd5ecb" class="abe-section-row" style="background-color: #ffffff;" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
<td style="text-align: center; vertical-align: top; font-size: 0; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;" align="center" valign="top"><!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
  <table width="100%" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
    <tr>
<![endif]--> <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
  <td width="600" valign="top" id="abe-column-block-64e15064-a1f1-4d5b-9b3a-0a34fe1eb9db-outlook-only" class="abe-column-block-outlook-only" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; padding: 15px;">
<![endif]-->
<div class="abe-column-block" id="abe-column-block-64e15064-a1f1-4d5b-9b3a-0a34fe1eb9db" style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; display: inline-block; font-size: 16px; vertical-align: top;" data-block-type="FancyBlockColumn" data-block-id="">
<div class="abe-column-block-padding" id="abe-column-block-64e15064-a1f1-4d5b-9b3a-0a34fe1eb9db-padding" style="padding: 15px;">
<table style="table-layout: fixed; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-wrap: break-word; text-align: left; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;" role="presentation" border="0" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" align="center">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
<h1 style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; text-align: right; font-size: 18px; font-family: 'times new roman', times; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 15px; line-height: 120%;" align="right"><font size="5">Cargo Systems Messaging Service</font></h1>
<div class="govd_hr">
<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<h2 style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 140%; font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 20px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">CSMS # 70050970 - Certain Canadian Products Excluded from Importation into the United States; Presidential Proclamations 11061, 11062, and 11063</h2>
<div class="govd_hr">
<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<p>The purpose of this message is to provide guidance on the Presidential Proclamations 11061, 11062, and 11063:</p>
<p>&ldquo;<a href="https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/09/excluding-certain-canadian-alcoholic-beverages-from-importation-into-the-united-states-in-response-to-continued-discrimination-against-the-commerce-of-the-united-states-with-respect-to-alcoholic-bever/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Excluding Certain Canadian Alcoholic Beverages from Importation into the United States in Response to Continued Discrimination Against the Commerce of the United States with Respect to Alcoholic Beverages,</a></p>
<p>&ldquo;<a href="https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/09/excluding-certain-canadian-products-from-importation-into-the-united-states-in-response-to-continued-discrimination-against-the-commerce-of-the-united-states-with-respect-to-motor-vehicles/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Excluding Certain Canadian Products from Importation into the United States in Response to Continued Discrimination Against the Commerce of the United States with Respect to Motor Vehicles</a>,&rdquo; and</p>
<p>&ldquo;<a href="https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/09/excluding-certain-canadian-products-from-importation-into-the-united-states-in-response-to-continued-discrimination-against-the-commerce-of-the-united-states-with-respect-to-dairy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Excluding Certain Canadian Products from Importation into the United States in Response to Continued Discrimination Against the Commerce of the United States with Respect to Dairy.&rdquo;</a></p>
<p><strong>GUIDANCE:</strong><br />Effective September 29, 2026, at 12:01 a.m., Eastern Time, certain covered products of Canada identified in the Annexes to Presidential Proclamations 11061, 11062, and 11063 are excluded from importation into the United States. Exclusion from importation precludes covered products from admission into a Foreign Trade Zone or bonded warehouse, in-bond transportation, and entry for consumption. As of 12:01 a.m. Eastern Time on September 29, 2026, any entry containing covered products will be unconditionally rejected by U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP). The attached annexes outline the list of HTSUS classifications subject to exclusion.</p>
<p>Covered products imported prior to September 29, 2026, 12:01 a.m. Eastern Time, remain eligible to be entered for consumption. Such covered products, if entered into a bonded warehouse or admitted into a Foreign Trade Zone prior to exclusion from importation going into effect, may be withdrawn for consumption and will be subject to the 50 percent<em> ad valorem</em> duty under Presidential Proclamations 11046, 11047, and 11048, as applicable. The attached annexes outline the list of HTSUS classifications subject to exclusion.</p>
<p>As of 12:01 a.m. Eastern Time on September 29, 2026, covered products will be unconditionally rejected and denied entry by CBP. Entries filed in ACE which contain covered products that have not been released will be cancelled as of September 29, 2026 at 12:01 a.m.</p>
<p>Covered products include certain commodities under Harmonized Tariff Schedule of the United States (HTSUS) headings 0404, 1702, 1703, 2202, 2203, 2204, 2205, 2206, 2207, 2208, and 8711.</p>
<p><strong>Alcoholic Beverages</strong><br />For alcoholic beverages, the import exclusion applies only where the merchandise meets any applicable scope limitation listed in the <a href="https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ANNEX-I-ALCOHOL.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Alcohol Annex</a>. Where the scope limitation states &ldquo;Packaged,&rdquo; the exclusion applies only to products packaged in bottles, cans, boxes, kegs, or other similar direct-to-consumption containers. Alcoholic beverages that do not meet an applicable scope limitation are not subject to the import exclusion and remain subject to the applicable 50 percent ad valorem duty under Proclamation 11046.</p>
<p><strong>ACE Cargo Release</strong><br />Pursuant to the implementation of Presidential Proclamations 11061, 11062, and 11063, CBP will update the ACE Cargo Release and e214 Foreign Trade Zone (FTZ) admissions messaging on September 29, 2026 at 12:01 am. Filers attempting non-compliant submissions will trigger system rejects and receive the following error codes:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>239</strong> &ndash; HTS NOT ALLOWED FOR COUNTRY OF ORIGIN (for e214 FTZ admission)</li>
<li><strong>335</strong> &ndash; HTS NOT ALLOWED FOR COUNTRY OF ORIGIN (for Cargo Release)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>ACE Entry Summary Update/Create</strong><br />CBP will update the ACE Entry Summary Update/Create messaging on September 29, 2026 at 12:01 am. Filers attempting non-compliant submissions will trigger system rejects and receive the following error code:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>886</strong> &ndash; HTS PROHIBITED FOR CO</li>
</ul>
<p><br /><strong>Foreign Trade Zones</strong> <br />Any covered products that were admitted into a Foreign Trade Zone prior to 12:01 a.m. Eastern Time on September 29, 2026, may be withdrawn for consumption at the 50 percent<em> ad valorem</em> duty imposed under Proclamations 11046, 11047, and 11048, as applicable.</p>
<p><b>Contact information:</b></p>
<p>For questions regarding Section 338 entry filing, contact the Office of Trade at <a href="mailto:TradeRemedy@cbp.dhs.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TradeRemedy@cbp.dhs.gov</a>.</p>
<p>If you encounter any errors in filing an entry summary, contact your CBP client representative or the ACE Help Desk.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
