<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
<h1 style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; text-align: right; font-size: 18px; font-family: 'times new roman', times; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 15px; line-height: 120%;" align="right"><font size="5">Cargo Systems Messaging Service</font></h1>
<div class="govd_hr">
<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<h2 style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 140%; font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 20px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">CSMS # 69902241 - New Error Code for e214 Foreign Trade Zone Submissions Set to Deploy September 17, 2026, and Updates to CATAIR Appendix P and FTZ CATAIR</h2>
<div class="govd_hr">
<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<p>On September 17, 2026, U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) will implement a new error code for e214 Foreign Trade Zone (FTZ) admissions in the Automated Commercial Environment (ACE) Production environment. This change is currently available in the ACE Certification environment.</p>
<p>The<i> ACE Appendix P &ndash; e214 FTZ Admission Error Codes</i> document was updated to add the following error code:</p>
<ul>
<li>238 - FIRMS CODE NOT APPROVED FOR DIRECT DELIVERY</li>
</ul>
<p>In addition, the <i>ACE Foreign Trade Zone</i> chapter of the CBP and Trade Automated Interface Requirements (CATAIR) was updated to clarify existing requirements. The documents can be found, respectively, in the &ldquo;Appendices&rdquo; and &ldquo;Current Capabilities&rdquo; sections of the <a href="https://www.cbp.gov/trade/automated/catair" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ACE CATAIR</a> webpage.</p>
<p>Trade parties that have an ACE Secure Data Portal (ACE Portal) account with the FTZ Operator sub-account view are encouraged to use the ACE Portal to verify the Zone ID, FIRMS Code, and Port Code information associated with the FTZ Sites they operate.</p>
<p>For technical questions, please contact your assigned CBP Client Representative or your local Port of Entry. For questions about this CSMS please contact <a href="mailto:CREM@cbp.dhs.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CREM@cbp.dhs.gov</a>.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
  </td>
<![endif]--> <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
  </tr>
  </table>
<![endif]--></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
<![endif]--></td>
<td style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">&nbsp;</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>]]>
      </description>
    </item>
