<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<h2 style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 140%; font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 20px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">CSMS # 69763204 - Cargo Release Condition Codes Documents has been Posted to cbp.gov</h2>
<div class="govd_hr">
<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<p>The Cargo Release Condition Codes documents have been posted to cbp.gov with the following changes pertaining to Entry Type 13. These changes are expected to be deployed to U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) Automated Commercial Environment (ACE) Production environment on September 22, 2026.</p>
<p>&bull; Error code changes pertaining to Entry Type 13<br />o Error code 334 was added<br />o Error code 325 was removed</p>
<p>The Cargo Release Condition Codes document is available in the Supporting Documents section on cbp.gov: https://www.cbp.gov/document/guidance/cargo-release-condition-error-codes</p>
<p>For any technical questions regarding this update, please contact your assigned Client Representative.</p>
<p>Other questions regarding Cargo Control and Release should be directed to CREM@cbp.dhs.gov. For questions or concerns regarding Entry Summary, please email Entry Summary, Accounts and Revenue Division (ESAR) at esar@cbp.dhs.gov</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
  </td>
<![endif]--> <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
  </tr>
  </table>
<![endif]--></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
<![endif]--></td>
<td style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">&nbsp;</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>]]>
      </description>
    </item>
