<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
<h1 style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; text-align: right; font-size: 18px; font-family: 'times new roman', times; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 15px; line-height: 120%;" align="right"><font size="5">Cargo Systems Messaging Service</font></h1>
<div class="govd_hr">
<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<h2 style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 140%; font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 20px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">CSMS # 69680973 - Registration Now Open: U.S. Customs and Border Protection September 2026 Trade Enforcement Webinars</h2>
<div class="govd_hr">
<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<p>U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) is pleased to announce that registration is now open for two upcoming trade enforcement webinars this September. These complimentary quarterly sessions are designed to educate the public on how to effectively report suspected trade violations and file Enforce and Protect Act (EAPA) allegations using the Trade Violations Reporting (TVR) tool.</p>
<p><b>Webinar Schedule:</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b><a href="https://inevent.com/en/WebinarUSCustomsandBorderProtection-1739306113/TVRQ4/hotsite.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Trade Violations Reporting (TVR) Webinar:</a></b> Tuesday, September 22, 2026, at 1:00 p.m. ET</li>
<li><b><a href="https://inevent.com/en/WebinarUSCustomsandBorderProtection-1739306113/EAPAQ42026/hotsite.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Enforce and Protect Act (EAPA) Webinar:</a></b> Thursday, September 24, 2026, at 1:00 p.m. ET</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Registration:</b> Registration is free and open to the public; however, advance registration is required to attend. Please register at <a href="https://www.cbp.gov/trade/stakeholder-engagement/webinars" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://go.dhs.gov/4i4</a>.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
