<h2 style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 140%; font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 20px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">CSMS # 69511296 - Information: Quota Bulletin 26-405 2027 Cotton Note 9</h2>
<div class="govd_hr">
<div class="govd_hr_inner"><hr /></div>
</div>
<p>Quota Bulletin 26-405 2027 Cotton Note 9 has been published on our webpage at the following link: <a href="https://www.cbp.gov/trade/quota/bulletins/qb-26-405-2027" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Quota Bulletin 26-405 2027 Cotton Note 9</a></p>
<p>Commodity:</p>
<p>Cotton card strips, the product of any country or area including the United States, as provided in the Harmonized Tariff Schedule of the United States (HTSUS), Chapter 52, Additional United States Note (AUSN) 9.</p>
<p>Quota Period:</p>
<p>September 20, 2026, through September 19, 2027</p>
<p>Opening Date:</p>
<p>Monday, September 21, 2026</p>
<p>All entries submitted after 12:01 a.m. local port time and prior to 8:30 a.m. Eastern Time (ET) and on the opening date will receive an entry time of 8:30 a.m. for quota qualification purposes. If the total for any HTSUS group exceeds the limit at 8:30 a.m. ET, all accepted entries will be prorated.</p>
<p>Questions regarding this message should be referred to Headquarters Quota and Agriculture Branch at <a href="mailto:HQQUOTA@cbp.dhs.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HQQUOTA@cbp.dhs.gov</a>.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
